Five small, independent release-polish fixes (no version bump; the 0.1.0 cut
stays deferred):

1. Non-interactive banner → stderr. bin/forge.js printed "Non-interactive mode:
   using … agent selection" to STDOUT, prepending the forge.issue.v1 JSON envelope
   of kernel issue commands so non-TTY agents/CI could not parse default (no --json)
   output. Route both banner lines to console.error (stderr). Verified: `forge issue
   create --title=A --type=task` (no --json) now emits pure parseable JSON on stdout,
   banner on stderr.
2. Filesystem-class warning: confirmed already on stderr — lib/kernel/fs-class.js
   emits via console.warn (stderr), with no console.log path. No change needed.
3. AGENTS.md: reword the State Management line so the Kernel is described as the
   default issue-state authority and Beads as the opt-in import/export/projection
   compatibility layer, matching the shipped model.
4. migrate-dry-run: replace the literal "TODO/BLOCKER: …" strings in the user-facing
   dry-run report with neutral wording ("fixture corpus not available/not found …").
5. CHANGELOG [Unreleased]: backfill Keep-a-Changelog entries for the three merged
   PRs — #270 (Fixed: forge export projects kernel issues to git-tracked JSONL),
   #269 (Changed: pre-merge is an embedded doc gate, not a stage/command), #271
   (Changed: engines.node >=22.16.0, stray test excluded from the tarball, doc-gate
   documented). No version bump; no [0.1.0] section.

Test: test/bin/non-interactive-banner-stderr.test.js spawns `forge issue create`
(no --json) and asserts stdout is a banner-free forge.issue.v1 JSON envelope with
the banner on stderr. eslint --max-warnings 0 clean; migrate-dry-run, v2-fixture,
agents-md and docs-consistency suites green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
